WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
One student argues that John Hick's
theodicy successfully defends the goodness

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.770
of God.

3
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.070
Another argues that it fails.

4
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.220
Same question.

5
00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.510
Same scholars.

6
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.300
Opposite conclusions.

7
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:15.000
Yet both essays can reach the top band.

8
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:20.200
So how is it possible for two opposite
conclusions both to get top marks?

9
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.280
In this mission, you'll put
a statement under the lens,

10
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:27.270
hunting for strength words
such as most and proves.

11
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:30.710
Then you'll build an evaluative
paragraph rung by rung,

12
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.030
from a point to a
mini-judgement that links back.

13
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.770
Your mission: work out how opposite
judgements can both earn top marks.
